r and film critic, one of the pioneers of the new realist strain in British cinema during the 1950s and 1960s. Two of the best-known films he directed are Saturday Night and Sunday Morning (1960), a classic of kitchen sink realism, and the romantic period drama The French Lieutenant's Woman (1981).\n\n", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T15:46:13.976609+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 4462, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karel_Reisz"}], "uuid": "79b74507-0543-451a-9295-07a7945bf95c", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "1769", "external_references": [{"id": 24912, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q167023"}, {"id": 29721, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "2643759"}, {"id": 29722, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "n80112811"}, {"id": 29723, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-n80112811"}], "date_modified": "2023-08-01T15:46:17.166282+10:00"}, {"id": 8849, "name": "Selectparks", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2080764, "title": "acmipark", "work_id": 108732, "role": "creator", "role_id": 968, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": null, "date_of_death": null, "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "selectparks is a media laboratory currently based in Melbourne, Australia. selectparks was established in 1998 by Julian Oliver and now includes key members Chad Chatterton, Andrea Blundell and Rebecca Cannon. selectparks puts particular focus on the use of games as a platform for producing both Place and researching how sense, memory and action collaborate toward this unique effect. Out of a belief that games produce not only places but also new Public Places, the worlds of selectparks develop upon traditional concepts of public by offering both new mediums and sites for exchange. This aspect of selectparks¿ enquiry currently forms th